  data:  # eeff
    kind: work_item  # eeff
    title: "34 emitted Edge.meta keys are unregistered though axis_meta_keys claims exhaustiveness — 2 of them (enclosing_class, inherited_field_receiver; 158,375 edges) are written by make_unresolved_edge itself"  # eeff
    status: todo_hard  # eeff
    priority: 3  # eeff
    parent:  # eeff
    tags:  # eeff
    - axis  # eeff
    - analysis_quality  # eeff
    isbefore: []  # eeff
    duplicate_of: []  # eeff
    not_duplicate_of: []  # eeff
    pr_ref:  # eeff
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-27 by the fundamental concept audit of call_construct. Full\nwrite-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-call_construct_08272026.md\n\naxis_meta_keys.py's module docstring states that \"every meta key used by\nproducers / consumers across the codebase is declared once here with its\naxis\". That claim is false as shipped.\n\nMEASURED over 42 cached surveys (lutuh_scope_08242026), counting keys that\nactually appear on serialised Edge.meta: 70 distinct keys observed, registry\nholds 100, and 34 OF THE OBSERVED KEYS ARE UNREGISTERED.\n\nTwo of the 34 are written by the CORE HELPER ITSELF -- make_unresolved_edge\nin analyze/base.py, the function every language analyzer calls for an\nunresolved external:\n\n    enclosing_class            121,576 occurrences   analyze/base.py:895\n    inherited_field_receiver    36,799 occurrences   analyze/base.py:898\n\nOthers include binding, call_type, receiver_type_id, enclosing_class_id,\nevent, action, controller, visibility, event_name, publisher_event_type,\npublisher_framework, subscriber_event_type, subscriber_framework,\ntarget_path, handler_ref, mixin_name, component_name, events, has_slot_attr,\nsource_path, reference_path, event_type, controller_action, url_type,\nimport_form, package, import_name, attributes, client_directive,\ntarget_function, include_file, sourced_path, target.\n\nMETHOD NOTE -- A CONTAMINATION I HAD TO REMOVE. The first pass reported 36\nunregistered keys including `evidence_lang` at 1,025,469 occurrences. That is\nNOT a producer writing an unregistered key: ir.py:993 folds the TYPED FIELDS\nEdge.evidence_type and Edge.evidence_lang into the serialised meta dict at\nto_dict() time. Both are excluded above. Anyone re-running this measurement\nmust exclude exactly those two and no others -- to_dict folds nothing else.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS. The registry's stated purpose (docstring, \"Why a registry\nrather than free-form strings\", point 1) is producer/consumer coherence: a\nproducer typo like meta[\"framewok_role\"] silently yields None at the\nconsumer. That guarantee only holds for keys the registry knows about. Two\nkeys written by the central unresolved-edge helper on 158,375 edges are\noutside it.\n\nRELATION TO WI-vusot. WI-vusot asked whether to establish the parallel\nregistry at all; the registry now exists with 100 keys, so its KEY half\nshipped. This item is the drift that accumulated afterwards. The VALUE half\nof WI-vusot (its discussion point 3, \"Validation is two-level. Both the KEY\nand the VALUE matter\") is still unbuilt and is reported separately on that\nitem.\n\nSUGGESTED SHAPE. There is already a linter trio -- check-meta-write-discipline,\ncheck-producer-axis-coherence, check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration. The\ngap is an AST-walking check that every meta key literal emitted by a producer\nis registered, which is the same shape as the edge-type drift linter and\nwhich the audit playbook's Step 4 note predicts will find more than a manual\nsweep does. Registering the 34 is the first half; the linter is what stops\nthe 35th."  # eeff
    fields: {}  # eeff
- op: discuss  # 7897
  at: '2026-10-03T09:15:48Z'  # 7897
  by: agent  # 7897
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7897
  clock: 2  # 7897
  nonce: '7897'  # 7897
  message: "From WI-nakur's branch (jgstern-agent/fix/nakur, not merged), facts that bear on this item:\n\n1. More unregistered Edge.meta keys, not in the 34 listed: scip/edges.py writes scip_src_symbol, scip_dst_symbol, scip_relationship_flag; scip/calls.py writes scip_src_symbol, scip_dst_symbol, symbol_roles. axis_meta_keys registers only scip_kind (symbol meta). Checked by grep, not by a survey count (no relationship edges in any recorded run, so the edges.py keys have 0 occurrences today).\n2. The new hypergumbo_core.value_flow can enumerate dict KEYS: ModuleValueFlow(tree).resolve(expr, ((\"key\",),)) returns the keys of a dict display plus subscript-store / setdefault / update keys. Probe: meta={\"k1\": 1, \"k2\": 2} -> {'k1', 'k2'}. BUT a named dict passed as meta=edge_meta resolves to None: its escape rule counts the Edge.create(meta=...) call itself as an escape (the constructor is not a known non-mutating callee). A meta-key linter built on it must exempt the sink use (or resolve from the dict's own binding).\n3. Shapes that still hide values from the producer gates (statement-level narrowing, cross-module helpers, nested mutable collections) are listed on WI-gajoz-fasad-vojih-gomup-domar-zivis-durok-rudin; the same limits will apply to meta keys."  # 7897
- op: discuss  # fcb7
  at: '2026-10-03T10:47:23Z'  # fcb7
  by: agent  # fcb7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fcb7
  clock: 3  # fcb7
  nonce: fcb7  # fcb7
  message: "Agent run 2026-10-03, branch jgstern-agent/fix/lijaz (based on jgstern-agent/fix/nakur, not pushed). Commits: 7c7d53dac4 (value_flow), e2fdaaddc3 (gate + registrations).\n\nPremise re-verified: counting Edge.meta keys on the same 42 cached surveys (lutuh_scope_08242026) against the CURRENT registry gives 35 unregistered keys (the item's own list names 35, its title says 34), identical to the item's list. The static gate on the branch found 82 unregistered or wrongly-axised keys on the live tree, which include all 35.\n\nWhat shipped:\n- value_flow: the use being answered is not an escape; opt-in readers / known_empty; dict(m) passthrough; comprehension-filter narrowing. Side catch: clojure Symbol.kind 'multimethod' was unregistered (now AXIS_PENDING).\n- hypergumbo_core.meta_key_coherence: Edge(...)/Edge.create(meta=...) keys must be on edge_meta; post-hoc .meta writes must be registered on some axis. Ratchet axis \"Edge.meta key\" in scripts/check-producer-axis-coherence + test_live_tree_producer_axis_ratchet; baseline [\"route_path\"]. Unenumerable writes pinned by equality (1: ir.py dedup merge).\n- Registered 73 edge_meta + 6 symbol_meta keys as emitted (unaudited); symbol_roles and import_path moved to edge_meta.\nEvidence: ratchet red with 82 keys before registration, green after; mutation (unregister enclosing_class) -> ratchet red naming it; mutation (drop readers) -> pin red naming lua_ffi/pyffi/ruby_ffi/route_handler. Targeted smart-test (768 files): 24497 passed, 2 failed (a line-pinned citation and the spec symbol_meta count, both fixed and re-run: 68 passed), all changed sources 100% covered.\nNOT asserted: Symbol construction keys (WI-rorap-zafot-lunut-vogis-zudap-japat-jahon-sirak), cross-axis keys (WI-kuhoh-nihim-mozaj-napam-gimat-tupim-bivuj-kurum), reads, the axis of post-hoc writes. No fold-residue audit of the registered keys."  # fcb7
